## BUG FOUND & FIXED (F3 finding)
- **CSP blocked Supabase in production build**: `vite.config.ts` injected a static CSP
  meta with `connect-src 'self'` → all Supabase API calls blocked
  (`https://mhkieytinkgouhvwrmbp.supabase.co/auth/v1/otp` refused; 2 console errors;
  "Something went wrong" alert). Only manifested in production (dev exempt from CSP).
- **Fix**: `vite.config.ts` now derives `connect-src` from `VITE_SUPABASE_URL` at build
  time via `loadEnv` + `configResolved`. Rebuilt → dist CSP:
  `connect-src 'self' https://mhkieytinkgouhvwrmbp.supabase.co`
- Gates after fix: typecheck 0, lint 0 (pre-existing warnings only), test 128/128, build 0.

## Constraint discovered
- Supabase FREE tier + default emailer: email templates are NOT modifiable
  (API: "Email template modification is not available for free tier projects using the
  default email provider"). Default template sends a MAGIC LINK, not a 6-digit code.
- The app's 6-digit code-entry UI was already verified in prior sessions
  (ext-2-3-otp.png, mocked OTP). F3 used the REAL magic link to complete the real
  signed-in journey end-to-end.

